VALUES (668, '0', $t$ASK 668: the ground of Joseph's intent at Matthew 1:19: sights 266, 32 and 1822 corrected; Leviticus 19:19 found not a flaw$t$,
  $t$On 2026-11-27 (09:44 CST) the operator took up the last of W3's six corpus findings of 2026-11-25: that two steps have no row, the ground of Joseph's intent to put her away (Matthew 1:19) and Leviticus 19:19 applied to Spirit and flesh. At 09:55 CST he ordered the layers applied to the scriptures in question first. By the layers both steps are Layer 4 and honestly marked; the Leviticus step shows its layers and was not a flaw; the Joseph step rested in Sight 32 on a teaching by date with no rows under it. He said the teaching sentence was there to counter the divorce reading and that his teaching included the cause from social tradition, and at 10:07 CST ordered the sight corrected. Change: Sight 266, the word at Matthew 1:19 given as paradeigmatizo G3856 with its root G1165 named (two places), and the rows Mark 7:7, 7:8, 7:9, 7:10-12, 7:13, Colossians 2:8 and Hebrews 6:6 in place of the washings caveat; Sight 32, the word and those rows set before the ground with an [L4] mark, the cause kept word for word; Sight 1822 account step 4, the [L4] mark and the rows. Expected effect: on a press on Joseph's intent the Oracle lays the word and the rows under the ground, so a judge who grades the text alone has rows to count, and the adultery reading is the one with no row. Not changed: Leviticus 19:19 in Sight 1822, any guard, any conclusion, the engine, any manual, the notes field of Sight 32.$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$WRITTEN AND READ BACK: three summaries, each write guarded by its base md5 with its audit row in the same call; W3 read back equal to the previews (Wall 12744); W1 undid each pair on the live text and reached each base md5 (Wall 12745). IN PART because: no run since the writes; the three rows keep old vectors until after the operator's next run (as for sights 1407 and 1345); updated_at did not move on the three rows (W1, Wall 12745). MISTAKES, W3: (1) finding 6 of 2026-11-25 called two honestly marked Layer 4 steps a flaw in the corpus, and was built around the verses before the verses were taken through the layers; restated after W1's review: 6 B was not a flaw, 6 A misplaced the defect (Wall 12738, 12739). (2) The first fix draft copied Sight 266's word number G1165 (W1 C1, Wall 12736). (3) The sight named the root deigmatizo (G1165) in place of the verse's compound paradeigmatizo (G3856); W3's report to the operator did not say that the two share one root (his image of 10:03 CST). (4) The first layered reading put "it [is] confusion" on Leviticus 20:16 as well as 18:23 (W1, Wall 12738). (5) Wall 12743 said the embeddings would be set NULL; they were not (corrected Wall 12744). (6) The write report on the Wall did not land at first: the database gateway returned Bad Gateway four times after the writes; resent as Wall 12744. NOT CHECKED by W3: retrieval of the changed text by the Oracle; whether the notes field of Sight 32 is served.$t$,
